course: dictionary
lesson: 7079
title: Pause: a short stop
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pause can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a pause is a short stop or rest: «When you are excited, wait for a pause in the talk before you speak.» The talk stops for a moment, then carries on.
explain: As a verb, to pause means to stop for a little while and then go on. Test it by swapping in a clear meaning: «Free verse has no regular rhyme or beat, but the poet breaks the lines where the reader should pause.» Does "stop for a moment" fit? Yes, so pause means stop for a moment there.
explain: Look for clue words around the word. Short pause, pause for thought and without a pause all tell you the stop is brief. A pause is not the end: the talk, the poem or the video carries on afterwards.
fact: A pause is a short stop or rest, and then you carry on.
fact: To pause means to stop for a little while and then go on.
fact: Pressing pause on a video or game stops it, so you can start again from the same place.
fact: A comma in writing tells you to pause for a moment when you read.
fact: Phrases to know: a short pause, pause for thought, without a pause, pause button.
exercise: «When you are excited, wait for a pause in the talk before you speak.» What is a pause here? | A loud shout that stops everyone | A change to a different room | *A short stop in the talk | A brand new topic
exercise: Mia presses the pause button on her video. What happens? | *It stops, so she can start again from the same place | It starts again from the very beginning | It disappears from the screen | It gets louder and faster
exercise: «The poet breaks the lines where the reader should pause.» What does pause mean in a poem? | To read faster and faster | *To stop for a short moment before going on | To skip the whole line | To shout the last word
test: To pause means to | *stop for a little while and then go on | make a loud noise | start again from the very beginning | run away from a task
test: A comma in a sentence tells the reader to | *pause for a moment | stop reading for ever | skip the next word | read in a higher voice
exam: Which phrase means stopping to think before you answer? | without a pause | pause button | *pause for thought | free verse
